cff-version: 1.2.0
version: "0.2.1"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "forgetted: mid-conversation incognito mode for AI agents"
abstract: >-
  forgetted is an AI reliability tool that gives AI agents selective memory
  governance: inside a context-managed window the agent keeps full read context
  but writes to memory files, session logs, deliverables, and vector stores
  silently vanish and are cleaned up on exit. It treats non-persistence as a
  memory-governance primitive enforced in software, not as a prompt instruction.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Bosch Rodriguez"
    given-names: "Rolando"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-4896-1112"
    affiliation: "Hermes Labs"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/hermes-labs-ai/forgetted"
keywords:
  - "AI reliability"
  - "LLM reliability"
  - "silent failure modes"
  - "ambient assurance"
  - "agent memory governance"
  - "selective non-persistence"
  - "incognito mode"
  - "persistence-layer adapters"
